# CampusEats Catalogue – CS543 Web Services

## Project Description

This project implements a simple CampusEats Catalogue using Node.js and Express.js.

It provides a REST API to retrieve all menu items, fetch a single dish by ID, and add new dishes. A simple HTML and CSS frontend interacts with the REST API using JavaScript fetch().

The application stores menu data in an in-memory array.

## Technologies Used

- Node.js
- Express.js
- HTML
- CSS
- JavaScript
- REST API

## Project Structure

```text
catalogue/
│
├── server.js
├── package.json
├── package-lock.json
│
└── public/
    ├── index.html
    └── style.css
```

## API Endpoints

| Method | Endpoint | Description |
|---|---|---|
| GET | `/items` | Retrieves all menu items |
| GET | `/items/:id` | Retrieves a single dish by ID |
| POST | `/items` | Adds a new dish to the menu |

## HTTP Status Codes

| Status Code | Meaning | Usage |
|---|---|---|
| 200 | OK | Successful GET request |
| 201 | Created | Successfully added a new dish |
| 404 | Not Found | Requested dish does not exist |
| 422 | Unprocessable Entity | Required name field is missing |

## Request Handling

- `req.params.id` is used to get the dish ID from the URL.
- `req.query.veg` filters menu items by vegetarian status.
- `req.body` contains the data sent when adding a dish.
